  "caption": "Quinn lost to a pickle jar, a finger started catching like a stubborn light switch, and the shoulder got stiffer every week.\n\nKay's take: diabetes can make joints and tendons stiffer and raise the chance of frozen shoulder, trigger finger, carpal tunnel and tendon problems. Tendons may also heal more slowly — it's not just ageing, and there's plenty you can do.\n\nWhat can help: working with your GP or diabetes team on blood sugar, addressing stiff shoulders and hands early, expecting tendon rehab to take a bit longer, combining strength and aerobic exercise, and checking your feet every day.\n\nGet it checked if a shoulder keeps stiffening, a finger locks, your feet feel numb, or a foot wound is slow to heal.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
